      ],
      "text": "**Probably, if the air stays as it was this morning—but check again before you leave.** At 7:00 a.m. on Saturday, October 17, Kuching’s reported Malaysian Air Pollutant Index (API) was **65, “moderate.”** That is not an evening reading, and haze can change during the day. ([jerebumalaysia.com](https://jerebumalaysia.com/en/stations/kuching-sarawak/?utm_source=openai))\n\nIf the API is still moderate this evening and you feel well, a **short, easy ride** is a reasonable choice; avoid a hard workout or a long ride, especially if you have asthma or heart or lung disease. If the reading rises **above 100**, or the haze makes you cough or feel short of breath, ride indoors or postpone. Exercise increases the amount of polluted air you breathe. ([eqms.doe.gov.my](https://eqms.doe.gov.my/apims/main?utm_source=openai))\n\nThere’s a separate riding hazard: Malaysia’s weather service forecasts **afternoon thunderstorms and rain at night in Kuching**. Don’t ride if there’s lightning, and check the weather as well as the DOE’s APIMS reading just before setting out. ([met.gov.my](https://www.met.gov.my/forecast/weather/town/Tn187/))",
